# Physics receipt: Springs, the force-directed default, re-applied through the
# panel. Its signature is rest: no overlapping bodies and the energy gone
# once the spring has rung down.
assert title GRAPHSHELL H3 READY
assert snap ready == true
# The boot arrangement pauses the canvas; the receipt wants the law running.
dom click [data-command="toggle-physics"]
settle 1
assert snap physics-paused == false
# No arrangement: the boot Spiral's anchor springs would pull under every law.
select #gs-arrangement-select free
dom click [data-command="apply-arrangement"]
settle 1
assert snap layout == free
assert snap physics-law == spring.rapier
select #gs-physics-select spring.rapier
dom click [data-command="apply-physics"]
settle 1
assert snap physics-law == spring.rapier
assert snap physics-profile == law.springs
assert dom #gs-product-status Physics set to Springs
capture physics_springs_start
wait
settle 60
capture physics_springs_settled
wait
# The spring's own energy rings down within four seconds (a probe read
# 235 000 → 1 800 → 460). What remains is a slow outward drift of the two
# disconnected components against the centering boundary, a few pixels a
# second, so rest here means: the ring-down gone, nothing overlapping, and
# the graph not flying apart.
settle 300
assert snap physics-energy <= 500
assert snap layout-overlaps == 0
assert snap layout-spread <= 250
log physics springs receipt complete
